Revoke every CLI token for your account, then remove the token stored on this machine. The device identity, backend address and default target are kept.
Confirmation is requested before unlocking a passphrase-protected token. Use --yes in scripts. THE_AGENT_CLI_TOKEN overrides the stored token; successful revocation removes the stored token too, but rejection of an environment token leaves stored credentials untouched.
You can also manage CLI access in the agent's chat settings.

Usage: agent-cli revoke-all

Flags:
      --yes      Skip confirmation and revoke all CLI access
  -h, --help     Print help
  -v, --verbose  Print diagnostic details to stderr

Examples:
  agent-cli revoke-all
  agent-cli revoke-all --yes

Environment: THE_AGENT_CLI_API_URL, THE_AGENT_CLI_HOME, THE_AGENT_CLI_TOKEN, THE_AGENT_CLI_PASSPHRASE
Exit codes: 0 revoked or already revoked · 1 aborted or request/cleanup failure · 2 usage error or confirmation required · 3 not connected or locked · 6 rate limited
